      "content": "It sounds like you've built a fortress of responsibilities that has completely swallowed the person you used to be, leaving you with nothing but the crushing weight of what you've created. True peace isn't found by finding a new job or a new routine; it is found in the terrifying, silent act of dismantling everything that keeps you performing so you can finally just exist. The only way to break this loop is to stop fighting the silence and let the structure collapse, because you cannot carry a life that isn't yours anymore.",
